# Branch names

Before `git checkout -b` or `git switch -c`, pick a name that `pnpm lint:branch` accepts. Husky runs the same check on commit.

Pattern: `<project>/<type>/<kebab-description>`

- `project` is an `apps/` or `packages/` folder name, or `root` for repo-wide work
- `type` is one of: feat, fix, chore, docs, refactor, test, ci, hotfix, research, prototype

Examples: `amelie-engine-api/feat/team-bindings`, `skills-config/chore/sort-init`, `root/docs/branch-names`

`main` is only for integrating already-reviewed work. Leave the pre-commit hook enabled so the lint runs.
